{title: Beersheba}
{subtitle: Genesis 21:22–34}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm] [F] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[Bb]bimelech and Phicol came to me [F/A]
[Gm7]God is with [Eb]you in all your [Bb]deeds [F/A]
[Gm7]Swear to me by [F/A]God, do not [Bb]lie
Show the kind[Eb]ness that you [Bb]see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
I confronted him about the well
[F/A]His [Gm7]servants took it, he denied
[F]I [Eb]gave him sheep and cattle too
And a [Fsus4]covenant we made anew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Seven ewe lambs I set aside
[Eb]Witness that I dug this well
Beer[Gm7]sheba, where we swore
God’s [Eb]truth is [Fsus4]clear and [Bb]full [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Abimelech [Eb]asked what this [Bb]means [F/A]
[Gm7]These seven [Eb]lambs from my [Bb]hand
[F/A]Ac[Gm7]cept them as my wit[F/A]ness
That I [Bb]dug the well in the [Eb]land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
They re[Gm7]turned to the Philistine land
Phicol and the [Fsus4]king went away
I [Eb]planted a tamarisk tree
And [Fsus4]called on the Lord that [F]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Seven ewe lambs I set aside
[Eb]Witness that I dug this well
Beer[Gm7]sheba, where we swore
God’s [Eb]truth is [Fsus4]clear and [Bb]full
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The [Eb]Everlasting God is my name
Called up[Gm7]on in the land of Canaan
[Eb]Lived as a foreigner there
In His [Fsus4]care and His plan
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Seven ewe lambs I set aside
[Eb]Witness that I dug this well
Beer[Gm7]sheba, where we swore
[Eb]God’s truth [F]is clear and [Bb][Eb]full [Gm7][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Beer[Bb]sheba, the [Eb]place of oath
[Gm7]Faithful [Fsus4]is God in all [Eb]truth
{end_of_verse}
